WEBVTT

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:06.690
Listen up! Y'all are insects 
worth less than crap!

00:00:07.030 --> 00:00:08.220
You got that?!

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:09.280
Yep.

00:00:09.770 --> 00:00:11.640
Don't "yep" me!

00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:14.660
Who am I, your school teacher? Hey!

00:00:14.660 --> 00:00:17.990
Watch this! Hey! Are you watching?!

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:17.990
Are they gonna be okay?

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:27.300
<b>Drugstore</b>

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:27.300
<b>In Another World</b>

00:01:48.040 --> 00:01:51.960
<b>Today's Prescription: Part 1
Power Potion</b>

00:01:48.910 --> 00:01:51.960
The only responses I want to 
hear from y'all are "yes" and "no."

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:53.990
And end your sentences with "ma'am."

00:01:53.990 --> 00:01:54.900
Question.

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:55.510
What is it?

00:01:56.370 --> 00:02:01.720
Ms. Annabelle, I don't think it's very 
nice to call people insects or crap.

00:02:03.860 --> 00:02:05.910
Don't talk back to your superior officer!

00:02:05.910 --> 00:02:08.770
We'll start with ten laps around town!

00:02:08.770 --> 00:02:09.770
Huh?

00:02:10.040 --> 00:02:12.090
I'll be behind y'all.

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:15.330
If I catch up to you, 
I'll whack your butt with this!

00:02:15.330 --> 00:02:16.240
Got it?!

00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:22.870
Getting hit hurts. Why would you do that?

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:25.520
Doz, tell her.

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:26.660
Yes, ma'am.

00:02:27.020 --> 00:02:30.750
She does it so you insects will run fast!

00:02:29.350 --> 00:02:31.260
What?!

00:02:31.260 --> 00:02:32.240
Woof.

00:02:35.350 --> 00:02:37.970
You! Who said you could run now?

00:02:37.970 --> 00:02:38.550
Woof?

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:42.010
I'm running around town. You said so.

00:02:42.350 --> 00:02:45.960
First I'll give the signal, 
then you start running.

00:02:45.960 --> 00:02:48.150
That's right. Maintain discipline.

00:02:48.150 --> 00:02:50.690
"Walk in step" is the signal.

00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:57.400
The free-spirited Noela can't handle acting 
as part of a group or maintaining discipline.

00:02:57.610 --> 00:03:02.240
<b>Kirio Drugstore</b>

00:02:57.920 --> 00:03:02.240
<b>Yesterday</b>

00:02:58.300 --> 00:03:02.240
Reiji, could you make me a medicine 
that will make me stronger?

00:03:03.640 --> 00:03:07.420
It's not good to rely on 
medicines to fix everything.

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:09.520
But there's no other way.

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:10.580
Hey.

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:14.790
I came to pick up today's potions, 
since I was in the area.

00:03:15.080 --> 00:03:18.460
Ms. Annabelle... Hey, I know!

00:03:19.990 --> 00:03:21.110
What?

00:03:29.520 --> 00:03:32.050
Pick up the pace!

00:03:32.050 --> 00:03:34.150
Good luck, guys!

00:03:34.540 --> 00:03:36.480
Thank you.

00:03:36.480 --> 00:03:40.190
Reiji, I'll do my best.

00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:42.870
Woof?

00:03:44.300 --> 00:03:45.410
Where are you goin'?

00:03:49.020 --> 00:03:51.500
Hey, you! Don't break ranks!

00:03:52.120 --> 00:03:53.600
Noela, what is it?

00:03:53.600 --> 00:03:55.080
Woof.

00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:56.380
Huh?

00:03:56.810 --> 00:03:58.340
Run with us.

00:03:58.750 --> 00:04:03.080
Nah, I'm good. I don't want to get stronger.

00:04:03.080 --> 00:04:06.300
Just watching is boring. Run with us.

00:04:06.610 --> 00:04:07.930
Huh?

00:04:08.510 --> 00:04:12.810
But I was planning to take 
it easy and have a nap!

00:04:12.810 --> 00:04:13.890
Jeez...

00:04:16.020 --> 00:04:18.210
Mr. Reiji, you're running with us?

00:04:18.210 --> 00:04:19.500
Yeah...

00:04:19.500 --> 00:04:22.090
Reiji, let's do our best.

00:04:22.090 --> 00:04:23.820
No, wait...

00:04:24.420 --> 00:04:27.840
Hey, you're the only one fallin' behind!

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:29.850
S-Sorry!

00:04:29.850 --> 00:04:30.870
Too slow!

00:04:38.890 --> 00:04:41.580
Ow!

00:04:41.580 --> 00:04:45.220
Huh? But my boys like it when I hit them.

00:04:45.490 --> 00:04:48.930
I'm not like those perverts!

00:04:49.160 --> 00:04:50.940
Did you say something'?

00:04:50.940 --> 00:04:52.390
No, nothing.

00:04:53.190 --> 00:04:54.360
I want to go home.

00:05:00.570 --> 00:05:03.990
It's finally over...

00:05:04.250 --> 00:05:06.590
It's not over yet! Get up!

00:05:06.590 --> 00:05:09.910
Push-ups and sit-ups! One thousand each!

00:05:09.910 --> 00:05:11.400
What?!

00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:13.130
No way, no way, no way, no way!

00:05:14.590 --> 00:05:17.290
Reiji, where are you going?

00:05:17.290 --> 00:05:20.540
We promised we'd get stronger together.

00:05:20.540 --> 00:05:22.160
I never made that promise!

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:26.880
I'm not trying to become stoic and 
powerful like some kind of Super S**yan!

00:05:27.270 --> 00:05:30.850
Hey, Insect B! What are you slackin' off for?!

00:05:30.850 --> 00:05:32.810
<b>Insect B</b>

00:05:31.670 --> 00:05:32.810
<i>Insect B.</i>

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:35.430
<b>Insect M</b>

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:35.430
<b>Insect N</b>

00:05:33.100 --> 00:05:35.430
<i>Insect M, Insect N.</i>

00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:36.950
<i>Insect R.</i>

00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:37.290
<b>Insect R</b>

00:05:38.110 --> 00:05:42.900
I'm scared. Reiji keeps trying to run away.

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:44.990
Hey, she snitched on me!

00:05:45.240 --> 00:05:48.120
Who said you could leave the battlefield?!

00:05:48.120 --> 00:05:50.770
That's right! Fleein' from the 
enemy earns you a hundred beatings!

00:05:50.770 --> 00:05:52.840
Nothin' beats the captain's beatings!

00:05:52.840 --> 00:05:54.050
What a perv.

00:05:54.050 --> 00:05:55.580
Did you say somethin'?!

00:05:55.580 --> 00:06:00.000
Ma'am! This is an advanced 
tactical retreat, ma'am!

00:06:00.410 --> 00:06:03.050
I'll be the judge of that.

00:06:03.050 --> 00:06:07.550
But I'm on my way to develop a new 
medicine that aids muscle growth.

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:09.840
What? You can do that?

00:06:09.840 --> 00:06:10.760
Seriously?

00:06:10.760 --> 00:06:12.170
Yes, ma'am!

00:06:12.670 --> 00:06:17.660
Fine, then. Insect R, 
get to developin' that medicine.

00:06:17.660 --> 00:06:19.190
Yes, ma'am!

00:06:20.570 --> 00:06:24.780
Don't you think Ms. Annabelle is 
being extra nice to Mr. Reiji?

00:06:24.780 --> 00:06:25.760
Woof.

00:06:25.760 --> 00:06:27.010
I don't think it's right

00:06:27.010 --> 00:06:30.450
for a teacher to show special 
treatment to individual students.

00:06:32.540 --> 00:06:36.790
Bringing personal feelings into 
the brigade disrupts discipline.

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:44.800
It could even lead to discord. 
What do you think?

00:06:44.800 --> 00:06:45.940
Shut up!

00:06:45.940 --> 00:06:48.520
You're not qualified to 
give advice to the captain!

00:06:48.520 --> 00:06:51.340
In the first place, I don't remember 
givin' you permission to speak!

00:06:51.630 --> 00:06:55.680
I don't think it's right to 
always talk down to others.

00:06:56.950 --> 00:07:01.370
If you instruct people based on 
illogical emotional arguments,

00:07:01.370 --> 00:07:05.050
then your mercenary band can't be very good.

00:07:06.290 --> 00:07:08.370
Hey, Mina!

00:07:08.370 --> 00:07:11.660
Ms. Annabelle's taking time out 
of her schedule for you guys.

00:07:11.660 --> 00:07:13.370
Stop putting her on the spot.

00:07:14.850 --> 00:07:16.790
Understood.

00:07:17.110 --> 00:07:21.420
All right, insects! I want 
500 more from each of y'all!

00:07:21.700 --> 00:07:22.730
Huh?

00:07:22.730 --> 00:07:24.380
I can't!

00:07:24.680 --> 00:07:25.870
Yes, you can!

00:07:25.870 --> 00:07:29.660
That's right. This is a typical 
workout for a mercenary company.

00:07:29.660 --> 00:07:31.930
Yeah. We do this every day.

00:07:32.240 --> 00:07:33.960
What?

00:07:34.710 --> 00:07:37.560
Too slow! Too slow! Too slow!

00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:39.930
Too slow! Y'all are too slow!

00:07:39.930 --> 00:07:41.890
<b>Kirio Drugstore</b>

00:07:44.920 --> 00:07:48.400
They wouldn't have to work out 
so much if they could increase

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:51.740
their muscle mass more efficiently.

00:07:52.390 --> 00:07:53.700
What if I mix

00:07:53.700 --> 00:07:57.590
materials together using the Energy 
Potion I previously brewed as a base?

00:08:17.670 --> 00:08:19.170
Okay, it's done!

00:08:18.830 --> 00:08:21.600
<b>Power Potion</b>

00:08:19.920 --> 00:08:21.600
<i>Power Potion.</i>

00:08:22.050 --> 00:08:26.850
This should allow them to build muscle 
easily without working out so hard.

00:08:30.120 --> 00:08:33.820
It kind of tastes like vanilla. 
This'll go down easy.

00:08:36.350 --> 00:08:38.740
Hey, I finished the medicine.

00:08:46.960 --> 00:08:49.790
Huh?! What have you been doing?!

00:08:50.910 --> 00:08:52.980
<i>I'm glad I was about to get out of that.</i>

00:08:52.980 --> 00:08:55.520
Master! Master's back!

00:08:55.520 --> 00:08:58.250
Noela, did you already finish your training?

00:08:58.250 --> 00:08:59.420
Woof!

00:09:00.010 --> 00:09:03.200
Hey, you. Why don't you 
join my mercenary company?

00:09:03.200 --> 00:09:05.400
But she can't act as part of a group.

00:09:05.400 --> 00:09:07.230
She's too free-spirited.

00:09:07.710 --> 00:09:11.120
I'm not joining. I'd rather be with Master.

00:09:11.120 --> 00:09:12.280
There, there.

00:09:12.280 --> 00:09:13.610
Woof.

00:09:13.610 --> 00:09:17.660
Oh, right. Here. This is the medicine I made.

00:09:18.460 --> 00:09:21.210
It helps your muscles recover.

00:09:21.210 --> 00:09:25.540
If you drink it after working out, it should 
strengthen your muscles more efficiently.

00:09:26.910 --> 00:09:31.290
Huh. This'll really make 
it easier to build muscle?

00:09:31.290 --> 00:09:34.940
It's not very effective for 
people who are already muscular.

00:09:34.940 --> 00:09:36.630
After all, they've already got muscles.

00:09:36.630 --> 00:09:38.710
Then it's pointless.

00:09:38.710 --> 00:09:41.750
But beginners should see good results.

00:09:41.750 --> 00:09:43.640
That's great.

00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:50.120
Woof!

00:09:54.270 --> 00:09:57.220
It's sweet. Now I'm ripped!

00:10:02.930 --> 00:10:06.100
You won't get ripped that easily.

00:10:07.980 --> 00:10:12.290
Huh? What?!

00:10:12.290 --> 00:10:14.130
That worked fast!

00:10:16.490 --> 00:10:20.240
A-Are you okay, Noela? What is it?

00:10:20.910 --> 00:10:21.750
Master.

00:10:21.750 --> 00:10:22.720
Huh?!

00:10:23.690 --> 00:10:27.680
I can hear my biceps speaking.

00:10:27.680 --> 00:10:29.570
Those don't speak!

00:10:29.570 --> 00:10:32.760
That's something first-rate bodybuilders say!

00:10:32.760 --> 00:10:34.480
Also, has your voice gotten deeper?!

00:10:35.230 --> 00:10:38.150
I can hear them... I can hear them.

00:10:38.510 --> 00:10:41.820
"Make us even bigger. Work us even harder."

00:10:42.140 --> 00:10:46.010
N-Noela, come back!

00:10:46.010 --> 00:10:48.310
Is something wrong with Ms. Noela?

00:10:48.310 --> 00:10:51.890
Oh, Mina. I guess my new 
medicine was too effective.

00:10:51.890 --> 00:10:55.750
Apparently she's hallucinating 
that her biceps are speaking to...

00:11:04.790 --> 00:11:06.450
Did you drink it, too?!

00:11:06.450 --> 00:11:12.500
Yes. I was thirsty, 
so I gratefully accepted your gift.

00:11:14.520 --> 00:11:17.200
Ms. Noela can hear her biceps speaking?

00:11:17.200 --> 00:11:19.420
I wonder what happened to her.

00:11:19.420 --> 00:11:20.940
Huh?

00:11:20.940 --> 00:11:23.620
I can hear my abs speaking to me.

00:11:23.860 --> 00:11:26.830
You, too?! What happened to you?! Do you have any self-awareness?!

00:11:26.830 --> 00:11:29.540
And you're not hearing anything! 
That's a hallucination!

00:11:30.320 --> 00:11:34.310
I'm enraptured by these impressive muscles.

00:11:34.310 --> 00:11:39.550
"Let's show off the fruits of your hard work."

00:11:40.250 --> 00:11:43.260
That's what Mr. Six Pack is telling me.

00:11:43.760 --> 00:11:45.270
Who the heck is that?!

00:11:45.270 --> 00:11:47.520
Oh, they're marvelous.

00:11:47.520 --> 00:11:50.660
M-Mina, come back!

00:11:50.660 --> 00:11:52.690
Give me back the Mina I know!

00:11:59.730 --> 00:12:02.530
Yo! Your biceps are like mountains.

00:12:02.530 --> 00:12:05.990
Yo! Look at those abs. Is that a 
bar of chocolate on your stomach?

00:12:06.420 --> 00:12:10.750
I can't do it. Nothing can 
come between them now.

00:12:14.110 --> 00:12:16.040
I'll just leave Vivi alone.

00:12:16.600 --> 00:12:17.480
Woof.

00:12:18.060 --> 00:12:22.860
Um, Ms. Annabelle, about this Power Potion...

00:12:21.710 --> 00:12:22.860
Woof.

00:12:22.860 --> 00:12:26.640
Make sure you dilute it by adding 
a few drops to some water.

00:12:26.640 --> 00:12:27.710
Woof.

00:12:26.640 --> 00:12:28.280
G-Got it.

00:12:28.280 --> 00:12:30.390
We're not drinkin' that straight.

00:12:33.190 --> 00:12:36.480
<i>Their muscle high lasted for about an hour,</i>

00:12:36.480 --> 00:12:40.400
<i>after which their bodies 
finally returned to normal.</i>

00:12:45.020 --> 00:12:50.400
Reiji, the voices they heard 
must've been the muscle spirit.

00:12:50.400 --> 00:12:52.540
Yeah, whatever.

00:12:54.040 --> 00:12:57.130
You don't have to lose 
weight or get stronger.

00:12:57.980 --> 00:12:59.940
We're a pharmacy.

00:13:02.030 --> 00:13:04.550
If you say so, Mr. Reiji.

00:13:04.930 --> 00:13:06.290
I agree.

00:13:08.800 --> 00:13:14.190
<i>Another fun day in another world 
without muscles, blood, or fighting.</i>

00:13:16.940 --> 00:13:22.400
<b>Kirio Drugstore</b>

00:13:18.080 --> 00:13:22.400
<b>Today's Prescription: Part 2
RK Gene Fluid</b>

00:13:18.720 --> 00:13:22.400
Master, it's about me and Noela.

00:13:22.820 --> 00:13:24.670
Okay, what is it?

00:13:24.670 --> 00:13:30.700
Do you suppose it's possible that 
Ms. Noela has no interest in me?

00:13:31.020 --> 00:13:32.830
You're just now figuring that out?

00:13:32.830 --> 00:13:35.040
What?! It's true?!

00:13:35.040 --> 00:13:36.670
Yeah, of course.

00:13:37.100 --> 00:13:42.890
But she must recognize me as an individual. 
After all, I'm the Demon King.

00:13:42.890 --> 00:13:45.620
I doubt she even recognizes that.

00:13:45.620 --> 00:13:50.740
I'm afraid I've made no progress 
in my relationship with Ms. Noela.

00:13:50.740 --> 00:13:54.220
Why does it sounds like you're asking 
for legit relationship advice?

00:13:55.940 --> 00:13:59.060
So, you want to develop your relationship.

00:13:59.060 --> 00:14:01.380
Yes. Impressive as always, Master.

00:14:01.380 --> 00:14:05.780
You're intelligent enough to 
infer so much from so little.

00:14:07.360 --> 00:14:11.990
Workplace relationships are difficult 
no matter what world you live in.

00:14:12.350 --> 00:14:14.080
Anyway, Master,

00:14:14.080 --> 00:14:18.960
I'd like you to make a medicine that 
will make us progress past friendship.

00:14:18.960 --> 00:14:22.090
This isn't something medicine can fix.

00:14:22.090 --> 00:14:23.980
I'm not asking to be lovers.

00:14:23.980 --> 00:14:28.120
Just something to make us more 
than friends, but not quite lovers...

00:14:28.120 --> 00:14:29.880
Easier said than done.

00:14:31.320 --> 00:14:36.400
Okay, fine. I wouldn't call it 
developing your relationship,

00:14:36.400 --> 00:14:39.060
but I can help you speak to 
each other as colleagues.

00:14:40.610 --> 00:14:43.100
Master!

00:14:43.100 --> 00:14:47.450
Despite everything you say, 
you always help me!

00:14:45.940 --> 00:14:47.450
Give me a minute.

00:14:50.840 --> 00:14:54.280
That said, I don't have a plan.

00:14:55.480 --> 00:15:00.220
Hey, Noela. You always stay home on 
days Ejil comes to the store, right?

00:15:00.220 --> 00:15:02.170
Woof? What about it?

00:15:02.550 --> 00:15:04.150
Do you dislike Ejil?

00:15:05.630 --> 00:15:07.580
I don't dislike Ejil.

00:15:07.580 --> 00:15:09.220
Really? That's surprising.

00:15:09.580 --> 00:15:12.180
I have an instinctive aversion to Ejil.

00:15:12.180 --> 00:15:13.580
Hah!

00:15:12.320 --> 00:15:15.890
<b>[Sad News] 
Instinctive Aversion</b>

00:15:13.580 --> 00:15:15.890
<i>Sad news: Instinctive Aversion.</i>

00:15:15.890 --> 00:15:18.770
An aversion is different 
from disliking someone.

00:15:18.770 --> 00:15:19.570
Woof.

00:15:19.570 --> 00:15:23.330
But what exactly does it mean to have 
an instinctive aversion to someone?

00:15:23.710 --> 00:15:31.860
Well, an aversion to their appearance, 
behavior, expressions, smell, hygiene,

00:15:32.110 --> 00:15:37.830
and manner of speech is probably what 
you'd call an instinctive aversion.

00:15:38.220 --> 00:15:39.050
Woof.

00:15:39.050 --> 00:15:41.660
In other words, you dislike 
everything about him.

00:15:44.020 --> 00:15:47.380
What do you find distasteful, specifically?

00:15:47.380 --> 00:15:49.740
The way he laughs. His overconfidence.

00:15:49.740 --> 00:15:52.690
Well, he is the top demon.

00:15:52.690 --> 00:15:55.620
And he fawns on me. I hate that.

00:15:57.890 --> 00:16:00.500
That's because you're so cold to him.

00:16:00.500 --> 00:16:03.600
Also, his smell. He smells 
different from you.

00:16:03.970 --> 00:16:07.030
His smell? Is it because he's a demon?

00:16:07.030 --> 00:16:10.570
I can't tell at all, but you can?

00:16:10.570 --> 00:16:14.570
I like your smell. I don't like Ejil's smell.

00:16:14.570 --> 00:16:17.190
A person's smell is important.

00:16:17.190 --> 00:16:20.060
Huh... His smell, huh?

00:16:20.060 --> 00:16:24.250
Daughters often instinctively 
dislike their father's smell.

00:16:24.250 --> 00:16:26.380
That was true in Ms. Elaine's case.

00:16:28.610 --> 00:16:32.880
Oh, yeah. They say that's got 
something to do with pheromones.

00:16:34.670 --> 00:16:36.780
Okay, I'll give it a shot.

00:16:39.410 --> 00:16:44.390
What smells a person likes or dislikes 
is determined on a genetic level.

00:16:44.980 --> 00:16:48.740
So I should make something 
that includes genes that smell

00:16:48.740 --> 00:16:52.820
pleasant to Noela—in other words, my genes.

00:17:02.830 --> 00:17:04.520
Okay, it's done!

00:17:04.730 --> 00:17:11.480
<b>RK Gene Fluid</b>

00:17:05.290 --> 00:17:11.310
<i>RK Gene Fluid. A potable 
fluid containing RK's genes.</i>

00:17:12.270 --> 00:17:17.740
If you sprinkle this over your food and 
eat it, my genes should enter your body.

00:17:18.630 --> 00:17:23.730
Like your genes, your body odor is related 
to what you eat, so it's perfect.

00:17:23.730 --> 00:17:26.470
In other words, I should 
drink all of this medicine.

00:17:26.470 --> 00:17:27.300
No!

00:17:27.300 --> 00:17:27.310
Huh?

00:17:27.670 --> 00:17:31.400
Listen, drinking all of it at 
once would have no effect.

00:17:31.400 --> 00:17:32.980
You want to eat food with this on it

00:17:32.980 --> 00:17:35.960
and slowly swap out the cells in your body.

00:17:36.560 --> 00:17:37.950
Slowly?

00:17:38.450 --> 00:17:42.680
After a week, your body odor 
should be pleasant to Noela.

00:17:42.680 --> 00:17:43.740
Woof.

00:17:42.890 --> 00:17:45.290
I-Impressive, Master!

00:17:43.740 --> 00:17:45.290
Woof.

00:17:45.630 --> 00:17:48.290
H-How can I thank you?

00:17:48.290 --> 00:17:53.250
Don't worry about it. It's the manager's job 
to maintain a pleasant work environment.

00:17:53.250 --> 00:17:55.720
I'll serve you forever, Master!

00:17:55.720 --> 00:17:58.590
Okay, okay, I get it.

00:18:11.310 --> 00:18:12.520
Woof?

00:18:12.520 --> 00:18:14.190
<b>Kirio Drugstore</b>

00:18:12.520 --> 00:18:14.190
<b>1 Week Later</b>

00:18:14.190 --> 00:18:16.530
Master, I finished all the medicine!

00:18:16.850 --> 00:18:19.510
All right. Then let's perform an experiment.

00:18:19.510 --> 00:18:20.740
An experiment?

00:18:20.740 --> 00:18:26.420
It's time for the first "Which One Is 
Mr. Reiji? Smell and Guess" event!

00:18:28.230 --> 00:18:29.680
Mina, what are you doing?

00:18:29.680 --> 00:18:31.850
What happened to you, woman?

00:18:31.850 --> 00:18:33.940
Mina, there's no need to get so excited.

00:18:33.940 --> 00:18:36.930
I-In that case, you should've said so!

00:18:36.930 --> 00:18:41.830
N-Now I look like a crazy 
person who got too excited!

00:18:41.830 --> 00:18:45.370
That's exactly what you are. 
You were totally ecstatic.

00:18:49.360 --> 00:18:51.200
Master, what are we doing?

00:18:51.200 --> 00:18:55.850
We're playing a game in which you 
try to guess which one is me

00:18:55.850 --> 00:19:00.370
based on smell alone out of me, Ejil, 
and a tomato covered in my new medicine.

00:19:00.370 --> 00:19:04.140
Woof. I won't get your smell wrong, Master.

00:19:04.140 --> 00:19:06.620
Okay, Noela. You're going to be blindfolded.

00:19:10.610 --> 00:19:12.690
Here's your blindfold.

00:19:12.690 --> 00:19:13.290
Woof.

00:19:17.050 --> 00:19:21.430
Out of A, B, and C, please 
guess which one is Mr. Reiji.

00:19:28.580 --> 00:19:30.550
Well, Ms. Noela?

00:19:30.550 --> 00:19:32.100
Woof?

00:19:32.450 --> 00:19:36.360
<i>Wow. Noela was so confident, 
but she's hesitating.</i>

00:19:36.360 --> 00:19:40.320
<i>In other words, when we're talking about 
smell, Ejil and I aren't that different.</i>

00:19:40.540 --> 00:19:44.400
Ms. Noela, have you figured 
out which one is Mr. Reiji?

00:19:44.400 --> 00:19:48.310
C? B? Woof...

00:19:54.480 --> 00:19:55.940
I got it!

00:19:55.940 --> 00:19:58.400
Then please declare your answer.

00:19:58.400 --> 00:20:00.210
Master is C!

00:20:04.510 --> 00:20:09.150
I got it right! Praise me, 
Master! Lots of praise!

00:20:09.150 --> 00:20:10.430
Okay, okay.

00:20:13.000 --> 00:20:15.700
But you did hesitate, Ms. Noela.

00:20:15.700 --> 00:20:16.580
Woof.

00:20:16.580 --> 00:20:18.930
I'm impressed you figured it out in the end.

00:20:18.930 --> 00:20:20.770
I wasn't sure if it was B or C.

00:20:20.770 --> 00:20:23.810
But B was panting.

00:20:23.810 --> 00:20:25.700
I knew right away that it was Ejil.

00:20:25.700 --> 00:20:27.070
Panting?

00:20:27.940 --> 00:20:34.460
When I saw Ms. Noela fervently 
smelling me, I couldn't help myself.

00:20:37.380 --> 00:20:39.340
So you're just a pervert!

00:20:39.620 --> 00:20:43.630
However, the medicine you 
made is the real deal.

00:20:43.630 --> 00:20:49.820
If I pour that over myself every day, 
then Ms. Noela will smell me every day!

00:20:53.690 --> 00:20:56.410
Ejil, <i>that's</i> your problem.

00:20:56.410 --> 00:20:58.820
Come, Ms. Noela.

00:20:58.820 --> 00:21:04.070
Right now I smell just like our master.

00:21:04.070 --> 00:21:04.700
Woof.

00:21:05.070 --> 00:21:06.590
I don't like Ejil.

00:21:08.940 --> 00:21:12.920
Listen, Noela. Ejil says he 
wants to get along with you.

00:21:14.700 --> 00:21:18.860
You both work at the same store. Don't you 
think it'd be better if you got along?

00:21:19.190 --> 00:21:22.530
In that case, fine.

00:21:22.530 --> 00:21:24.920
Then shake hands and make up.

00:21:26.790 --> 00:21:28.280
Ms. Noela...

00:21:28.630 --> 00:21:30.850
This must be tsundere behavior.

00:21:31.140 --> 00:21:31.990
Woof.

00:21:32.840 --> 00:21:38.060
Ejil, that's exactly why 
she doesn't like you.

00:21:38.800 --> 00:21:43.010
<i>Despite everything, Noela and Ejil 
started getting along a little better.</i>

00:21:43.990 --> 00:21:45.650
<b>Closing Time</b>

00:21:46.080 --> 00:21:47.110
Kirio Drugstore.

00:21:47.350 --> 00:21:48.280
Thank you...

00:21:48.280 --> 00:21:50.240
...for visiting...

00:21:50.530 --> 00:21:52.440
...again today.

00:21:52.440 --> 00:21:54.080
Woof.

00:22:00.460 --> 00:22:04.920
<b>Next Customer</b>

00:22:02.180 --> 00:22:04.920
I don't get it!

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:40.250
<b>Illustration by: sara</b>
